.TH GERANTD.CONF 5 2026-11-04 garnish "garnish manual"
.SH NAME
gerantd.conf \- what gerantd hands out to VMs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I ~/.config/garnish/gerantd.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR gerantd (1)
reads this file once, at startup; restart it after a change
.RB ( "systemctl \-\-user restart gerantd" ,
which shuts running VMs down). The file is optional, and so is every
setting. The syntax is that of
.BR garnish\-vm.conf (5).
.SH [Pool] SECTION
.TP
.BI CIDs= low \- high
The vsock context IDs given to VMs. A VM gets the lowest free one, and gives
it back when it stops. Default: 3\-99.
.TP
.BI DNS= addresses
At most two DNS servers, given to every guest on its kernel command line.
Unset, guests use the host's resolver: passt forwards the queries its
guests send to 10.0.2.3, and
.B gerantd
those NAT guests send to their gateway, to the first nameserver in
.IR /etc/resolv.conf .
Empty: no DNS servers.
.SH [Manager] SECTION
.TP
.BI StopTimeoutSec= seconds
How long a guest gets to shut down after the power button before crosvm is
stopped. Default: 30.
.PP
The NAT guests' addresses are set for all users in
.BR garnish\-network.conf (5).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gerantd (1),
.BR garnish\-vm.conf (5),
.BR garnish\-network.conf (5)
